   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Admission-rate sensitivity analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Admission rate is added only as a disclosed sensitivity analysis. Muse and Muse (2024, pp. 35–37) treat admission rate as a selectivity indicator but document that selectivity measures are missing for many institutions. The same problem is material here. Only 1,466 of 2,894 institutions report `ADM_RATE`, and the reporting subset contains 908 private nonprofits, 503 public institutions, and only 55 for-profits.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two models are estimated on exactly that restricted sample. The first repeats Model 3 without admission rate. The second adds admission rate. Comparing them separates the effect of adding selectivity from the effect of changing the estimation sample. This sensitivity model does not replace the full-sample Model 3."
   ]
